// =============================================================================
// core/hash/legacy/mod.vr — cryptographic by design, BROKEN in practice
// =============================================================================
// Layer: 1 (depends on core primitives only)
// =============================================================================
//

// Nothing here is a free choice. A module lands in `legacy` when a
// wire protocol mandates the exact bytes and the protocol's security
// does not rest on the broken property. Every call site must be able
// to state which protocol requires it.
//

//  * `sha1` — collision resistance is DEAD (SHAttered, 2017;
//    chosen-prefix collisions since 2020). Preimage resistance still
//    stands, which is why RFC 6455 may keep using it: the WebSocket
//    accept-key is a handshake echo that derives no security
//    property from the digest. Never use SHA-1 for signatures,
//    certificates, commitments or deduplication — use
//    `core.hash.crypto`.
//

// This module exists so that the dependency is visible in a mount
// line and in review. It must never become a convenience.
//

// =============================================================================

@arch_module(
    foundation: Foundation.ZfcTwoInacc,
    stratum: MsfsStratum.LFnd,
    lifecycle: Lifecycle.Definition
)
module core.hash.legacy;

public module sha1;
